5:{ev:["The crew sees a giant white squid.","Stubb kills the Pequod's first whale.","He eats a steak at midnight while sharks feed.","The crew strips the blubber and boils the oil.","Gabriel on the Jeroboam warns Ahab about Moby Dick.","Stubb begins to suspect Fedallah of being the devil."],keys:["squid","kills","steak","strips","warns","devil"]},
6:{ev:["Two whale heads hang from either side of the ship.","Tashtego falls into the sperm whale's head.","Queequeg dives in and saves him.","The Pequod races the German ship Jungfrau and wins.","The ship enters a grand armada of whales.","Ishmael's boat drifts into a calm center among mothers and calves."],keys:["hang","falls","dives","races","armada","calm"]},
7:{ev:["Pip jumps from Stubb's boat and is left alone at sea.","Rescued at last, Pip loses his mind.","Stubb tricks a French captain out of a whale full of ambergris.","The try-works burn all night.","Each sailor reads a different meaning into the doubloon.","Captain Boomer of the Samuel Enderby warns Ahab about his stump."],keys:["alone","rescued","tricks","burn","meaning","stump"]},
8:{ev:["The carpenter builds Ahab a new ivory leg.","Queequeg falls seriously ill.","He has the carpenter build him a coffin.","Queequeg decides not to die and recovers.","He turns the coffin into a sea-chest.","Ahab has the blacksmith forge a harpoon tempered in blood."],keys:["builds","ill","coffin","recovers","chest","blood"]},
9:{ev:["Fedallah prophesies that only hemp can kill Ahab.","A violent typhoon strikes the Pequod.","Ahab grips burning fire on the mast and defies the storm.","Starbuck considers killing the sleeping Ahab and cannot.","The compass is reversed and Ahab makes a new one.","Ahab smashes the quadrant in anger."],keys:["prophesies","typhoon","defies","considers","compass","smashes"]},
10:{ev:["A life-buoy is lost overboard.","Queequeg's coffin is sealed and rigged as a replacement.","The Rachel's captain begs Ahab to help search for his lost son.","Ahab coldly refuses to help.","Ahab tells Starbuck about his wife and forty years at sea.","Ahab almost yields, then looks at Fedallah."],keys:["lost","sealed","begs","refuses","wife","yields"]},
11:{ev:["Ahab himself sights Moby Dick and wins the doubloon.","On the first day, the whale bites Ahab's boat in two.","Three boats are wrecked on the second day.","Fedallah is dragged down with the line and lost.","Ahab's ivory leg snaps during the fighting.","Starbuck calls it madness; Ahab calls it fate."],keys:["sights","bites","wrecked","dragged","snaps","fate"]},
12:{ev:["Fedallah's corpse is found lashed to the whale's back.","Moby Dick rams the Pequod and sinks it.","Ahab darts his last harpoon into the whale.","The hemp line catches Ahab around the neck.","The ship goes down with all hands.","Ishmael alone survives, floating on Queequeg's coffin."],keys:["corpse","rams","darts","neck","down","survives"]}
